{"term":"wykorzystanie","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_exploitation","concept":"sexual_exploitation","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":70,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual exploitation or abuse; the act of using another person for sexual purposes without free and informed consent, typically involving a power imbalance.","english_term":"sexual exploitation","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Standalone 'wykorzystanie' means 'use' or 'exploitation' generically; sexual meaning requires context or the full compound 'wykorzystanie seksualne'."}
{"term":"zgoda seksualna","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"consent","concept":"sexual_consent","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":0,"technical":85,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":65,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual consent; the voluntary, informed, and ongoing agreement to participate in sexual activity.","english_term":"sexual consent","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Adoption of this compound has grown significantly in Polish public discourse post-MeToo (~2017); before then the concept was rarely named as an explicit term."}
{"term":"bez zgody","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"non_consent","concept":"non_consent","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":0,"technical":60,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Without consent; used in legal, clinical, and journalistic contexts to describe sexual acts performed without the other party's agreement.","english_term":"without consent","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Bez zgody' is a general Polish phrase ('without permission/agreement') repurposed in sexual-rights and legal discourse; not a fixed technical term but universally understood in context."}
{"term":"wymuszenie seksualne","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_coercion","concept":"sexual_coercion","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":80,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual coercion; the use of pressure, manipulation, or threats to compel another person into sexual activity.","english_term":"sexual coercion","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Legally distinct from 'gwałt' (rape); covers non-physical pressure and manipulation short of physical force; appears mainly in legal texts and NGO materials."}
{"term":"zastraszanie seksualne","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_intimidation","concept":"sexual_intimidation","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":75,"recognition_pct_current":50,"recognition_pct_peak":50,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual intimidation; the use of threatening behavior or language to frighten or coerce another person in a sexual context.","english_term":"sexual intimidation","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Less common than 'molestowanie seksualne' or 'przemoc seksualna'; appears primarily in legal and academic texts rather than everyday speech."}
{"term":"przemoc seksualna","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_violence","concept":"sexual_violence","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":80,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual violence; any act of a sexual nature committed against a person without consent, including rape, assault, and coercion.","english_term":"sexual violence","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Standard umbrella legal and journalistic term; widely used by NGOs and in media coverage of rape and sexual assault cases in Poland."}
{"term":"nadużycie seksualne","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"sexual_abuse","concept":"sexual_abuse","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":80,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sexual abuse; the act of subjecting another person to unwanted sexual acts, especially within a relationship of trust, authority, or dependency.","english_term":"sexual abuse","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Carries connotation of ongoing or systemic abuse rather than a single incident; frequently used in contexts of clergy abuse, domestic violence, and child protection."}
{"term":"wyruchać","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":90,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":95,"recognition_pct_peak":95,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Perfective crude slang verb meaning to fuck someone; to have sex with someone, framed as conquest or a completed act.","english_term":"to fuck (someone)","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Perfective aspect of 'ruchać'; 'wyruchał ją' = 'he fucked her.' 'Ruchać' is among the most common Polish crude sex verbs, comparable in frequency to 'pierdolić'."}
{"term":"zaciukać","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":35,"recognition_pct_peak":45,"peak_year":2015,"regional":null,"definition":"Youth slang verb for having sex; to fuck someone, with a crude or aggressive connotation.","english_term":"to bang, to screw","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primarily identified in teen/youth registers ca. 2010–2018; now declining. The base verb 'zaciukać' also means to stab/kill in some dialects, which may intensify the aggressive connotation in sex usage."}
{"term":"fiknąć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":40,"recognition_pct_peak":40,"peak_year":null,"regional":"PL-south","definition":"Regional youth slang perfective verb for having sex; to have a fuck, often implying a casual or quick encounter.","english_term":"to shag, to have a quickie","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primarily southern Polish regional usage; 'fiknąć' literally means to flip or somersault, repurposed as sex slang. Not spreading nationally; stable within its regional register."}
{"term":"napierdalać się","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude reciprocal imperfective verb meaning to fuck each other; vigorous or sustained mutual sexual intercourse.","english_term":"to fuck each other","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From 'pierdolić' with na- intensifier prefix and reflexive -się marking mutual action; one of many Polish crude sex verbs in the 'pierdolić' family. The na- prefix adds intensity."}
{"term":"rypać","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Regional vulgar imperfective verb meaning to fuck; to have sex with someone with crude and often aggressive connotation.","english_term":"to fuck","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Less universal than 'ruchać' or 'pierdolić'; weighted toward rural and working-class registers; known nationally but used actively mainly in regional speech communities."}
{"term":"rypnąć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":65,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Perfective form of rypać; to fuck once, to have sex with someone on a single completed occasion.","english_term":"to fuck (once), to shag","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Perfective aspect implies a completed single act; 'rypnął ją' = 'he fucked her.' Used interchangeably with rypać where perfective aspect is required."}
{"term":"rypanie","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_generic","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":65,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Verbal noun from rypać; the act of fucking; crude regional slang for sexual intercourse as an ongoing activity.","english_term":"fucking (noun)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Nominalized form; 'ostre rypanie' = 'hard fucking.' Less widespread than 'ruchanie' (from ruchać) or 'pierdolenie' (from pierdolić), which dominate nationally."}
{"term":"dać się rypnąć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"sexual_permissiveness_pejorative","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":60,"recognition_pct_peak":60,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to let oneself be fucked'; passive construction implying willing sexual submission, used pejoratively about someone regarded as sexually available or loose.","english_term":"to let oneself get fucked","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The 'dać się' (to allow oneself) construction frames the subject as passive and consenting; typically slut-shaming when said about a woman, but can be neutral in first-person use."}
{"term":"wdupczyć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"anal_sex","concept":"anal_sex","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Very crude slang verb meaning to fuck in the ass; to perform anal intercourse, emphasizing penetrative insertion into the anus.","english_term":"to fuck (someone) in the ass","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Compound from 'w' (into) + 'dup-' (ass, from 'dupa') + verbal suffix -czyć; the anal meaning is fully transparent to Polish speakers from the morphology."}
{"term":"nabzdyczyć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":30,"recognition_pct_peak":30,"peak_year":null,"regional":"PL-east","definition":"Perfective regional crude slang verb meaning to fuck someone; to have sex with someone.","english_term":"to fuck, to screw","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Rare; primarily eastern Poland; perfective counterpart to 'bzdyczyć.' Etymology unclear — possibly onomatopoeic or from eastern dialect roots. Largely unknown outside its origin region."}
{"term":"bzdyczyć","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"intercourse_aggressive","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":85,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":25,"recognition_pct_peak":25,"peak_year":null,"regional":"PL-east","definition":"Imperfective regional crude slang verb meaning to fuck; habitual or ongoing sexual intercourse.","english_term":"to fuck (habitual/ongoing)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Rarer than its perfective counterpart 'nabzdyczyć'; both terms are confined to eastern Polish regional speech and virtually unknown to younger urban speakers nationally."}
{"term":"dać się pierdolić","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"acts","subcategory":"intercourse_crude","concept":"sexual_permissiveness_pejorative","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to let oneself be fucked'; passive construction implying sexual willingness or submission; used pejoratively about someone regarded as sexually permissive.","english_term":"to let oneself get fucked","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From 'pierdolić', one of the most vulgar Polish sex verbs; the 'dać się' construction is the key marker of passivity and willing submission; standard in slut-shaming register."}
{"term":"żebrać o seks","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexual_desperation","concept":"sexual_desperation","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to beg for sex'; describes someone so sexually desperate that they make their need humiliatingly explicit.","english_term":"to beg for sex","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Not a fixed idiom but a transparent compositional phrase; used to mock or pity someone whose sexual desperation has become socially visible. Implied subject is usually male."}
{"term":"głodna tego","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexual_craving","concept":"intense_sexual_craving","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hungry for it' (feminine grammatical form); idiom expressing intense female sexual craving or horniness.","english_term":"gagging for it, horny (female subject)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The feminine adjective 'głodna' grammatically marks the subject as female; the male counterpart is 'głodny tego.' 'Tego' (genitive of 'to') is a vague deictic standing in for sex."}
{"term":"głodny tego","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexual_craving","concept":"intense_sexual_craving","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hungry for it' (masculine grammatical form); idiom expressing intense male sexual craving or horniness.","english_term":"gagging for it, horny (male subject)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The masculine adjective 'głodny' grammatically marks the subject as male; the female counterpart is 'głodna tego.' Both forms use 'tego' as a vague genitive deictic for sex."}
{"term":"lecieć na kogoś","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"attraction","concept":"amorous_desire","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to fly toward someone'; very common Polish colloquial idiom meaning to fancy, be attracted to, or have a crush on someone.","english_term":"to fancy someone, to be into someone","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Leci na nią' = 'he's into her.' Not inherently sexual — covers romantic attraction and celebrity infatuation as well as sexual desire. One of the most widely used attraction idioms in Polish."}
{"term":"mieć na kogoś chrapkę","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexual_craving","concept":"lust","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'to have an appetite for someone'; Polish idiom expressing strong desire or lust directed at a specific person.","english_term":"to have the hots for someone, to lust after someone","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"More intense than 'lecieć na kogoś'; 'chrapka' implies hungry appetite. The phrase is also used for non-sexual coveting (wanting someone's job or possession), but in sexual contexts maps to lust."}
{"term":"chrapka","lang":"pl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"desire_arousal_descriptors","subcategory":"sexual_craving","concept":"lust","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Noun meaning strong appetite or craving; in sexual contexts, lust or desire for a specific person.","english_term":"lust, appetite (for someone)","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Rarely appears standalone; almost always in the fixed phrase 'mieć chrapkę na kogoś/coś.' Not exclusively sexual: covers ambition, greed, and covetousness generally."}
